<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mstislav of Tmutarakan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1036">1036</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Mstislav Vladimirovich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mstislav of Tmutarakan was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-the-great">Vladimir the Great</a> who ruled the principality of Tmutarakan on the Taman peninsula. In 1024 he defeated his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-the-wise">Yaroslav the Wise</a> at Listven, after which they divided the Rus' lands along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a>, with Mstislav ruling the east from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chernigov">Chernigov</a>. On his death in 1036 without surviving heirs his lands passed to Yaroslav.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mstislav-of-tmutarakan.jpg" alt="Mstislav of Tmutarakan" width="320" height="145" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nicholas Roerich · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mstislav_and_Rededia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
